              "subject": "[PATCH] btrfs: downgrade the reflink source inode lock",
              "date": "2026-09-09T17:28:12Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch downgrades the lock on the source inode during reflink operations from exclusive to shared, reducing latency for concurrent readers. The change also adds a new flag to indicate when an inode is being used as a reflink source, which allows dio writes to take the VFS inode lock in shared mode instead of exclusive. This improves performance by avoiding unnecessary blocking of other shared lock users of the src file.",
